<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Canberra funds A$22 mln homeless youth plan.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Canberra funds A$22 mln homeless youth plan.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Education Minister Amanda Vanstone said on Thursday the government would provide A$22 million over the next two years to help homeless youth.</p>
<p>The job placement, employment and training programme would help nearly 8,000 young people Australia-wide, targeting those aged between 15 and 19, Vanstone said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Other at risk groups, such as refugees, ex offenders, wards of the state or those exiting wardship may also get help from the programme,&quot; Vanstone said.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 66-6 273-2730</p>
